== BotBuffer.xml
== NPC-bot party buffers: summon-controlled characters that
== cast a support skill (Mana Shield, Greater Damage, etc) on
== a player who trades with them, optionally for a Zen/PCPoint
== fee and/or gated behind VIP or Gens Family requirements.
== Loaded by GameServer via ObjBotBuffer::LoadXML().
== Reduced 2026-08-25 from ~50 duplicate entries (one Elf and
== 49 near-identical copies of the same Soul Master bot spread
== across Lorencia) down to the original 2: one Elf buffer and
== one Soul Master buffer, at the user's request.
== Modify only if you know what you're doing!
============================================================

### BotBuffer::Config::Bot ###
	Index             0-99, fixed.
	Class             eClass value (see Item.h). 0,1,2=DW,SM,GM;
	                  16,17,18=DK,BK,BM; 32,33,34=Elf,ME,HE;
	                  48,49,50=MG,DM; 64,65,66=DL,LE; 80,81,82=SU,BS,DS.
	Enabled           1 = this bot spawns. 0 = skipped.
	ColorName         PK-level color tint applied to the bot's name (0-7).
	Zen               Zen fee charged per buff. 0 = free.
	PCPoint           PCPoint fee charged per buff. 0 = free.
	MaxLevel          Player's character level must be <= this to use
	                  the bot.
	Name              Bot's display name, max 10 characters.
	Map/X/Y/Dir       Spawn location.
	OnlyVip           1 = requires AccountLevel > 0 (VIP) to use.
	ActiveGensFamily  1 = enforces the GensFamily requirement below.
	ContributionGens  Minimum GensContribution required (when
	                  ActiveGensFamily = 1).
	GensFamily        Required Gens Family (1 Vanert, 2 Duprian) when
	                  ActiveGensFamily = 1.

	Child <Equipment> - up to 9 <Item> slots (0-8, see comment below)
	worn by the bot for its visual appearance only:
		Slot    0=Sword 1=Shield 2=Helm 3=Armor 4=Pants
		        5=Gloves 6=Boots 7=Wings 8=Pet
		Type    Item section (matches Item.xml).
		Index   Item sub-index within that section.
		Level   Item +Level.
		Opt     Excellent/extra option value.

	Child <Skills> - up to 5 <Skill> entries applied (in order) to the
	player when they trade with this bot:
		Index   Skill/effect ID (see SkillManager.cpp's BotBuffer switch
		        - 28 Greater Damage, 27 Greater Defense, 16 Greater Mana
		        Shield, 64 Critical Damage, 48 Greater Life, 217
		        Reflect, 82 Magic Circle, 129 Greater Ignore Defense
		        Rate, 130 Fitness).
		Time    Buff duration in minutes.
		Power   Buff magnitude (%).

STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

